WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.500
These days, major movie studios mark their
spots on the release schedule years ahead

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.070
of time, and it seems like audiences have
to wait forever once a film is announced.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:12.980
But before you know it, we'll all be buying
our tickets for summer 2018's hottest big

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.579
screen blockbusters.

00:00:14.579 --> 00:00:19.051
From superhero sequels to explosive crime
thrillers to mind-bending horror flicks, it

00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:22.190
looks like there's a whole lineup of films
that are well worth the wait.

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:26.160
Among the dozens of promising projects slated
for release, here are some of the movies that

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.490
are going to hit big.

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:29.490
Hereditary

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:33.920
According to critics, Hereditary isn't your
run-of-the-mill fright flick, it's a movie

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.820
that's going to leave you shaken to your very
core.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:41.040
Starring Toni Collette, Hereditary tells the
story of a family dealing with grief after

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.010
the passing of a grandmother.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:46.840
Unfortunately, Grandma might not be gone,
and she might not be so friendly.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:51.899
The AV Club described the film as "pure emotional
terrorism," and it's got an ending that Daily

00:00:51.899 --> 00:00:54.809
Dead compared to movies like Carrie and The
Witch.

00:00:54.809 --> 00:00:59.090
In other words, prepare yourself for some
cinematic trauma.

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:00.440
Ocean's Eight

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:05.070
Using the same basic premise of Ocean's Eleven,
a group of quirky cons pull off an incredibly

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:08.070
elaborate heist, Ocean's Eight has done a
gender swap.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:12.470
A movie like this relies on the likability
of its cast, similar to the George Clooney

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:16.640
version, Ocean's Eight has assembled one of
the very best teams in recent memory.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:20.450
With an actor lineup this awesome, it's seems
likely that Ocean's Eight will totally be

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:22.820
able to hold its own against Steven Soderbergh's
classic.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:24.120
"Do we have to steal stuff?"

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.220
"Yes."

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:26.640
Incredibles 2

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:32.320
14 years after the release of The Incredibles,
our crime-fighting family is ready to save

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.490
the world yet again, and Incredibles 2 is
going to pick up right where the old one left

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:37.490
off.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:41.640
As for the plot, the exact details are hard
to find, but we know Craig T. Nelson's Mr.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:46.180
Incredible will be staying at home, watching
after his superpowered baby, while Holly Hunter's

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:50.510
Elastigirl goes on an adventure and stretches
her superpowers to new limits.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:54.470
Bob Odenkirk and Catherine Keener have also
joined the cast, and while we don't know who

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:59.000
they're playing yet, there's a good chance
they might be some sort of dastardly duo.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:00.240
"Bye Sweetie…"

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.380
"I'll watch the kids, no problem."

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.460
Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:10.750
When Jurassic World roared into theaters in
2015, it quickly became the fourth highest-grossing

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:15.120
film of all time, raking in nearly $1.7 billion
dollars.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:19.780
Now, with Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom,
not only will we get to see raptors run amok,

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:24.080
but we'll also watch an abandoned theme park
get blown to smithereens.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:29.050
Directed by J.A. Bayona, this blockbuster
promises to be an over-the-top spectacle,

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:31.910
complete with the return of Jeff Goldblum's
Ian Malcolm.

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:35.800
It's pretty safe to say Fallen Kingdom won't
go extinct at the box office.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:39.940
"Life finds a way."

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:42.830
Sicario: Day of the Soldado

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:47.540
You wouldn't necessarily think a movie like
Sicario needs a sequel, but rest assured,

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:50.740
Sicario: Day of the Soldado is in good hands.

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:55.630
Sicario scribe Taylor Sheridan, the genius
behind Hell or High Water and Wind River,

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:59.670
wrote the screenplay, resulting in what's
bound to be an incredible thriller.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:04.290
According to The Independent, director Stefano
Sollima promises a more cinematic film than

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:08.560
the first, featuring, quote, "an incredible
amount of huge action sequences."

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.350
We're also going to get a film that's far
darker than the first, with returning star

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:17.400
Josh Brolin describing the story as "severe,"
and Sheridan telling IndieWire that

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.640
"[Soldado] makes the first one look like a
comedy."

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:22.920
The First Purge

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:28.060
The Purge franchise has been picking off victims
and making political points since 2013, but

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:33.510
now, with The First Purge, we'll get an answer
as to how this night of bloodshed all started.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:38.161
Directed by newcomer Gerard McMurray and written
by franchise mastermind James DeMonaco, the

00:03:38.161 --> 00:03:41.600
newest film will take place before the Ethan
Hawke original.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:46.040
DeMonaco told Entertainment Weekly that the
cast will be 90 percent black, adding to the

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:48.360
film's socio-political message.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:53.040
Naturally, the film is set to hit theaters
on July 4th, when fireworks will light the

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:56.700
sky and blood will flow in the streets.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:58.230
Ant-Man and the Wasp

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:03.310
Audiences are in for a marvelous time when
Ant-Man and the Wasp arrives on July 6th.

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:07.760
With Peyton Reed returning to direct, both
Paul Rudd and Evangeline Lilly will be suiting

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.400
up as the titular heroes.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:14.130
Apparently, the pair will attempt to rescue
Michelle Pfeiffer's Janet van Dyne from her

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:16.750
decades-long adventure lost in the quantum
realm.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:18.060
Lilly told Vanity Fair,

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:23.950
"If we do succeed in Ant-Man and the Wasp,
then that does open a whole entire new multi-verse

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:26.150
to enter into and play around in."

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:30.900
In other words, things are going to get super
weird after Infinity War.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:32.730
The Equalizer 2

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:37.010
Ready to see a super assassin and hardware
expert dispose of some gangsters with gardening

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:38.010
tools?

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:42.590
Your dreams may very well come true on August
3rd, when Denzel Washington returns for The

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:44.180
Equalizer 2.

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:48.910
Re-teaming with director Antoine Fuqua, Washington
is making history here, starring in his very

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:50.190
first sequel.

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:54.470
There aren't a lot of plot details out there,
but come on, we're going to see Denzel destroy

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:57.220
a bunch of bad guys in incredibly creative
ways.

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:59.280
What more do you need to know?

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.220
Mission Impossible: Fallout

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:03.750
Tom Cruise's Ethan Hunt is at it again.

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:06.190
"Oh, you know, same old Ethan."

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:09.730
Director Christopher McQuarrie returns to
helm a sixth installment to the covert op

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:11.280
action-adventure series.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:15.810
McQuarrie has promised that we will, "[get]
to know who Ethan is in this movie," and that

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:20.350
our action hero will actually go on an emotional
journey, maybe that's why Michelle Monaghan

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:22.340
is returning as Ethan's old flame.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:26.260
In addition to a killer cast, we're super
psyched to see the crazy stunts Cruise and

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:27.720
McQuarrie have cooked up.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:32.170
Cruise trained for a year to prepare for some
truly insane action sequences, and we can't

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:37.320
wait until July 27th to see how the superstar
puts his life on the line this time.

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:38.580
The Meg

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:44.280
Cue the creepy music, because The Meg is an
ancient shark that's tormenting deep sea fishermen

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:48.430
in this adaptation of bestseller Meg: A Novel
of Deep Terror.

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:52.980
The film features Jason Statham as a rescue
diver who must help a stranded submarine and

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:56.110
its crew escape the teeth of the prehistoric
beast.

00:05:56.110 --> 00:06:00.610
Shark movies automatically earn creeping dread
just by their nature, but this flick looks

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:05.810
to take us into the depths of our fears, it's
literally dropping the distressed crew into

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:10.960
the deepest parts of the Pacific Ocean, so
we're in for an action-packed treat.

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:12.260
Captive State

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:17.340
John Goodman is revisiting the sci-fi genre
with Captive State, an alien invasion thriller

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:21.570
from Rupert Wyatt, the director who gave us
Rise of the Planet of the Apes.

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:25.540
According to the official plot description,
the film is set in Chicago "nearly a decade

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:28.740
after an occupation by an extra-terrestrial
force."

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:33.720
Captive State will focus on "the lives on
both sides of the conflict, the collaborators

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:37.980
and dissidents," and we can't wait for this
science fiction flick to invade movie theaters

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:40.550
on August 17th.

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:41.780
White Boy Rick

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:47.380
At only 14 years old, a Caucasian teenager
from Detroit named Rick Wershe Jr. was recruited

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.250
as a snitch by the FBI.

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:53.560
He went on to help the feds arrest some dangerous
drug lords, before becoming a big-time dealer

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:54.560
himself.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:59.530
A story this wild was just begging for someone
to make it into a movie, and fortunately,

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:02.840
White Boy Rick is set to hit theaters on August
17th.

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:07.139
As real-life Ricky's story recently took a
strange turn, it'll be interesting to see

00:07:07.139 --> 00:07:09.419
how these events will affect the film.

00:07:09.419 --> 00:07:15.030
White Boy Rick promises to be one of the craziest
true crime stories of the year.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:16.030
Mandy

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:19.350
It seems like Nicolas Cage's entire career
was leading to Mandy.

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:24.510
All the freaky faces, all the onscreen breakdowns,
all the awesome Nicolas Cage moments were

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:25.780
building up to this.

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:27.480
"Oh, yeah!

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:28.840
You put your right foot in.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:30.900
You take your right foot out.

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:35.139
You do the hokey-pokey and you f---ing work
it all out."

00:07:35.139 --> 00:07:40.180
The result is a big bloody of explosion of
LSD weirdness and battle axe action mixed

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:42.840
with rage, pain, and a lot of vodka.

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:47.591
Mandy finds Cage playing a man who embarks
on a revenge mission in a film that, according

00:07:47.591 --> 00:07:48.591
to The Verge,

00:07:48.591 --> 00:07:53.990
"...combines the most absurd aesthetic excesses
of '70s and '80s horror films with the most

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:57.170
absurd thespian excesses of Nicolas Cage."

00:07:57.170 --> 00:08:01.690
...which obviously makes Mandy sound like
one of the greatest movies ever made.

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:03.370
The Nun

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:08.080
The Conjuring series is quickly making its
case that horror movie franchises can also

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:09.660
become extended universes.

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:14.310
Following in the success of the franchise's
first spinoff, Annabelle, producers have given

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:19.290
the Demon Nun from The Conjuring 2 her own
film, titled simply The Nun.

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:25.120
The plot, which may be a prequel to The Conjuring
2, involves a priest who is called in to investigate

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:26.820
a nun's passing in Rome.

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:31.110
If there's anything we've learned about demonic
presences in Hollywood history, it's that

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:33.890
Italy tends to provide quite a creepy backdrop.

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:35.100
This'll definitely be one to watch.

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:39.480
(listening to metal for the first time)

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:41.500
Robin Hood

00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:47.070
We've had Errol Flynn, Kevin Costner, and
an animated fox.

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:51.050
Now it looks like Taron Egerton will don Robin
Hood's trademark green tights.

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:55.790
Robin Hood is going to be like a medieval
version of Batman Begins, showing us how Robin

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:59.200
of Locksley became Great Britain's most famous
bandit.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:03.960
According to Deadline, the movie will take
place after Robin returns home from the Crusades

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:08.390
only to find that Sherwood Forest is now "rife
with corruption and evil."

00:09:08.390 --> 00:09:12.550
Jamie Foxx, who's playing Little John, says
the movie, quote, "looks like you're watching

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:13.950
Zero Dark Thirty."

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:18.570
Taking Robin Hood in a dark direction is certainly
an interesting choice, and with the winning

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:24.180
combo of Egerton and Foxx, the upcoming action
flick could be one of 2018's most exciting

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:25.430
movies.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:27.550
The House with a Clock in its Walls

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:32.820
Eli Roth isn't really known for his kid-friendly
films, but he's looking to change things up

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:35.260
with The House with a Clock in its Walls.

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:39.770
Based on the classic children's book, this
Gothic fright flick tells the story of a 10-year-old

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:44.100
boy who's sent to live in a quiet Michigan
town with his uncle… who turns out to be

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:45.100
a warlock.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:49.750
There's also a witch next door, plus an apocalyptic
clock, hidden in the walls, of course, and

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:53.480
things get especially tricky when our hero
resurrects an evil being.

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:57.060
This spooky movie is set to scare kids on
September 21st.

00:09:57.060 --> 00:09:58.370
Thanks for watching!

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:00.960
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:02.950
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

